  "executive_briefing": "The mid-2026 outlook is defined by the imminent Senate floor vote on the Digital Asset Market CLARITY Act (H.R. 3633), which serves as a major catalyst for structural evolution across the crypto landscape. By resolving jurisdictional boundaries between the SEC and CFTC, this legislative milestone is unlocking institutional pathways that extend far beyond passive ETF storage. Institutional interest is actively transitioning toward secure, Bitcoin-native smart contract and decentralized finance (DeFi) layers, directly challenging Ethereum's long-standing virtual machine (EVM) hegemony. Concurrently, to support these multi-network environments, the industry is migrating from vulnerable custodial bridging models toward advanced, non-custodial omnichain and intent-based liquidity protocols, mitigating systemic risks for asset swaps between BTC and EVM-native ecosystems.",
